# Verify Before Done

Do not tell the user work is complete until verification passes for the areas touched by the change.

## Required checks

Run applicable commands and fix failures before finishing:

| Area changed | Command |
|--------------|---------|
| Frontend (`client/`, root `package.json`) | `npm run lint` |
| Frontend logic/components | `npm test` (root + `cd viz-lib && npm test` if viz-lib changed) |
| Production bundle | `npm run build` when webpack/config/deps changed |
| Backend (`redash/`, `requirements*.txt`) | `make backend-unit-tests` or `docker compose run --rm server tests` |
| Broad or uncertain scope | `make test` (lint + backend + frontend) |

## Workflow

1. Make the change.
2. Run the checks above that match the diff.
3. If a check fails, fix and re-run until green.
4. Only then report completion; mention which commands passed.

## Exceptions

- Pure documentation under `security-audit-2026/` with no code changes — no test run required.
- User explicitly says to skip verification for a draft or exploratory change.
- Environment blockers (Docker down, missing deps): say what failed to run and what still needs verification locally.

## Commit / ticket hygiene

When closing a slice of work, note verification in the commit message or Jira comment, e.g. `lint + jest + backend tests pass`.
